How to improve API Performence in .net

1️⃣ Optimize Database Access
Use async EF Core calls (await dbContext.Users.ToListAsync()).
Select only needed columns (.Select(x => new { x.Id, x.Name })).
Use AsNoTracking() for read-only queries to skip EF Core change tracking.
Add indexes to frequently searched columns in SQL.
Avoid N+1 queries by using Include() or projections.
Use stored procedures for heavy operations.
Cache frequent DB calls with IMemoryCache or Redis.

2️⃣ Reduce Payload Size
Use pagination for large result sets.
Compress responses (app.UseResponseCompression()).
Remove unnecessary properties from DTOs.
Return 204 No Content instead of an empty array.

3️⃣ Use Caching
In-memory cache for small, frequent reads.
Distributed cache (Redis, SQL Server) for multi-server setups.
Cache static data (dropdowns, configs, metadata).
Implement ETag / If-None-Match for conditional GET requests.

4️⃣ Middleware & Pipeline Optimization
Keep the middleware pipeline short.
Move expensive logging to background jobs.
Use UseRouting() → UseAuthentication() → UseAuthorization() → MapControllers() order.
Avoid unnecessary exception catching in global middleware (throw only when needed).

5️⃣ Use Asynchronous Processing

Async controllers & EF Core calls.
Background tasks for slow operations (IHostedService, Hangfire, Azure Functions).
Use message queues (RabbitMQ, Kafka) for heavy processing.

6️⃣ Minimize Serialization Cost

Use System.Text.Json instead of Newtonsoft.Json (faster).
Ignore null properties:
builder.Services.Configure<JsonOptions>(options =>
{
    options.SerializerOptions.DefaultIgnoreCondition = JsonIgnoreCondition.WhenWritingNull;
});

7️⃣ Connection & Resource Management

Use connection pooling (enabled by default).
Dispose DbContext, HttpClient, and streams properly.
Use IHttpClientFactory to avoid socket exhaustion.

8️⃣ Profiling & Monitoring

Use tools like dotMemory, dotTrace, Application Insights.
Find slow SQL with EF Core logging:
optionsBuilder.LogTo(Console.WriteLine, LogLevel.Information);

9️⃣ Scaling Strategies

Use Load Balancers & horizontal scaling.
Deploy behind CDN for static files.
Split monolith into microservices for high-load APIs.